{
  "_comment": [
    "Shared node-id cases, read by both packages/core/.../ids.py's tests and",
    "packages/types/src/node-ids.ts's tests. The two modules decode the same",
    "wire data, so a rule that holds in one and not the other is a live bug —",
    "and nothing but a shared list of cases can fail a build when they drift.",
    "",
    "kind:        the variant name, lowercased ('file', 'symbol', 'external', ...)",
    "file_path:   the file this id refers to, or null",
    "symbol_name: the symbol this id names, or null",
    "is_external: names code we do not own (third-party or framework)"
  ],
